 "generatorWeaknesses": [
  "Authored clues of a step with conditions are ignored (QuestTextService.generated): a condition always means a generated clue, so an authored 친구 or 집 line only works on an unconditional step.",
  "The validator only accepts the first taught concept when it lists the goal id among its items (covers are not looked at): spruce_sapling with the concept sapling is rejected, only oak_sapling passes, and that pair (PLANT, oak_sapling) is already at the limit of 2.",
  "The verb field of BREAK_BLOCK is limited to MINE/CHOP/HARVEST by the schema, so snow cannot be dug (파요) nor flowers picked (SNAP is only chosen by the verb table).",
  "PLACE_REL anchors need a block with a Korean name: water has none (\"the anchor minecraft:water has no Korean name\"), so 물 옆에 cannot be asked for.",
  "A tag anchor (#minecraft:flowers) is spoken as \"그것\" in PLACE_REL and as \"블록\" in BREAK_BLOCK; the ceremony line says 참나무 원목 where the clue says 통나무.",
  "The concept snow covers snow and snow_block, so CRAFT/BUILD of snow blocks reads \"눈을 만들어요\" and the ceremony \"눈 세 개로\"; the batch authors clue and finale for that trail.",
  "SKY OPEN is spoken with 하늘이 보이는 곳에서 (L3.neun_attr, a level 3 construction) and fails GrammarLadderTest at level 1; ROOFED (지붕 아래에서) is fine.",
  "The note block is rung with 울려요 (verb table family bells_and_notes); 쳐요 or 연주해요 would be more natural.",
  "Only about 4 spare authored finales: SentenceDumpTest wants more than 300 generated ceremony lines and the tree has 304 now. Two finales of this batch are authored (waldhaus, schneeballpfad).",
  "The pair limit (verbObjectMax 2) is already used up by PLACE torch/candle/note_block/red_bed, PLANT dandelion/poppy/oak_sapling, DRINK milk_bucket, EAT apple/bread and HANG_DOOR oak_door; the batch uses other objects (campfire, button, white_bed, birch_door ...).",
  "QuestScaffoldTest.theFinaleIsNeverOneOfTheTrailsOwnTasks depends on a root trail ending with PLACE_BLOCK chest (the scaffolder picks from tools/data/finales.json); briefpfad keeps that finale."
 ]
